  "type": "singleCorrect",
  "level": 1,
  "question": {
    "text": "Each of the two inputs $A$ and $B$ can assume values either 0 or 1. Then which of the following will be equal to $\\bar{A} \\cdot \\bar{B} ?$",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "2CG2p",
      "text": "$A+B$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "j1QZL",
      "text": "$\\frac{}{A+B}$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "5vXmD",
      "text": "$\\frac{}{A \\cdot B}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "23RhF",
      "text": "$\\bar{A}+\\bar{B}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "By using the de-Morgan's law\r\n$$\r\n\\overline{A+B}=\\overline{A \\cdot B}\r\n$$\r\nHence, option (b) is the correct.",
    "image": null
  },
